Description: Copy the selected tracks to a folder (DECKSMITHOS_COPY_ROOTS)
 [Library],copy_selected opens a dialog for the files of the tracks selected
 in any library view (also Browse): a folder tree whose roots are
 DECKSMITHOS_COPY_ROOTS ("CONSOLE=/storage/library:USB=/usb:USB2=/usb2"; a
 root listed in DECKSMITHOS_DRIVES only while a drive is mounted there), an
 optional new folder, COPY and CANCEL. Files are copied unchanged, each
 under a temporary name renamed when complete; a file of the same name in
 the folder is skipped; the free space is checked first (and the 4 GiB
 limit of FAT32). The copy runs in a thread at the lowest CPU and idle I/O
 priority and drops the copied data from the page cache. A drive is made
 writable for the copy with DECKSMITHOS_USB_WRITE_COMMAND <mount point> on,
 and read-only again with ... off. Copied files are added to the library.
 For a touch screen appliance without a file manager. Without the variable
 the control does nothing.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
